  <constraints>
    <constraint type="data-integrity">Must preserve existing article content (Purpose, Key Exports, Signals, Missing Signals) — only modify Dependencies, Dependents, and External Dependencies sections. Articles were generated by Story 6.1 and contain valuable reverse-engineered content.</constraint>
    <constraint type="accuracy">Import path resolution must handle: relative paths (./, ../), aliased paths (@/ from tsconfig.json), directory imports (resolve to index.ts/index.js), barrel re-exports (trace through to actual source). Incorrect resolution creates wrong edges.</constraint>
    <constraint type="architecture">External dependencies (npm packages) must NOT generate [[wikilinks]] — there are no wiki articles for npm packages. They are listed in a separate subsection for informational purposes only.</constraint>
    <constraint type="consistency">Wiki article slugs must use the -- convention from Story 6.1: src/utils/jwt.ts becomes code/src--utils--jwt.ts. Slug mismatches break graph edges.</constraint>
    <constraint type="dependencies">Runs after Story 6.1 completes. Reads .mycelium/bootstrap-manifest.json to map file paths to article slugs. Can run in parallel with Story 6.3 since they modify different wiki directories.</constraint>
  </constraints>

